{"type": "message", "id": "6ba6acc3", "parentId": "a9ccffd3", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T03:53:13.105Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_367f4756e0ce4461bc7b401e", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"adrenal cancer adrenocortical carcinoma annual cases US\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 935,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"886e85b4758e9aeb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAdrenocortical Carcinoma - StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf - NIH\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"886e85b4758e9aeb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK546580/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fcc48b349d1f9463\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAdrenocortical carcinoma represents a highly aggressive malignancy arising from the adrenal cortex, with an annual incidence of <strong>0.5 to 2 cases per million</strong> and a bimodal age distribution affecting young children and adults in midlife.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fcc48b349d1f9463\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 13, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e378abde5f1d9ab7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe Characteristics and Trends in Adrenocortical Carcinoma: A United States Population Based Study - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e378abde5f1d9ab7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6031252/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"77f171823bcbd050\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe annual incidence in our study was found to be <strong>1.02 per 1,000,000 populations</strong>. This is