    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a56271204b403c4a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAL 30,030 AZ 42,560 AR 19,700 CA 199,980 CO 29,020 CT 23,920 DE 7,680 FL\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a56271204b403c4a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/content/dam/cancer-org/research/cancer-facts-and-statistics/annual-cancer-facts-and-figures/2025/2025-cancer-facts-and-figures-acs.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e8bfdfa3542806c6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTable 4. Incidence Rates for Selected Cancers by State, US, 2017-2021 ... Dist. of Columbia ... Rates are per 100,000, age adjusted to the 2000 US standard population using 19 age groups, and adjusted for delays in case reporting. aExcludes appendix.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e8bfdfa3542806c6\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9ac6dc4b53b89678\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer statistics, 2025 - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9ac6dc4b53b89678\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39817679/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"896e97eb33587550\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEach year, the American Cancer Society estimates the numbers of new cancer cases and deaths in the United States and compiles the most recent data on population-based cancer occurrence and outcomes using incidence data collected by central cancer registries (through 2021) and mortality data ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"896e97eb33587550\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"31f108c7f5363503\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer statistics, 2026 - Siegel - 2026 - CA: A Cancer Journal for Clinicians - Wiley Online Library\\n<<<END_EXTER