100 cases. For each of the site-specific cancers we report, we have provided a table of the top 5 countries by ASR and then a table for yearly incidence (new cases).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"efea2b1914a563ff\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 28, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.wcrf.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"673f8cd9c922d8ae\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer Facts and Statistics | American Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"673f8cd9c922d8ae\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/research/cancer-facts-statistics.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1e78b47a2ac91442\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe American Cancer Society (ACS) projects the numbers of new cancer cases and deaths expected each year to estimate the contemporary cancer burden because cancer incidence and mortality data lag 2 to 4 years behind the current year. The regularly updated Facts &amp; Figures publications present the most current trends in cancer occurrence and survival, as well as information on symptoms, prevention, early detection, and treatment. ... ACS has published Cancer Facts &amp; Figures annually since 1951.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1e78b47a2ac91442\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "rarest cancers United States annual cases incidence per year", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 952, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"08ea0a2e17f0d1c4\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCancer Stat Facts: Common Cancer Sites - SEER\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"08ea0a2e17f0d1c4\">>>", "url": "https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/common.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"07a77ee819992ba0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCancer Statistical Fact Sheets are summaries of common cancer types developed to provide an overview of frequently-requested cancer statistics including incidence, mortality, survival, stage, prevalence, and lifetime risk.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"07a77ee819992ba0\">>>", "siteName": "seer.cancer.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2a1d2448989e1bfd\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCancer Statistics - NCI\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2a1d2448989e1bfd\">>>", "url": "https://www.cancer.gov/about-cancer/understanding/statistics", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e40a9e4c6e8f87a6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe Annual Report to the Nation on the Status of Cancer provides an annual update of cancer incidence, mortality, and trends in the United States.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e40a9e4c6e8f87a6\">>>", "siteName": "www.cancer.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a56271204b403c4a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAL 30,030 AZ 42,560 AR 19,700 CA 199,980 CO 29,020 CT 23,920 DE 7,680 FL\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a56271204b403c4a\">>>", "url": "https://www.cancer.org/content/dam/cancer-org/research/cancer-facts-and-statistics/annual-cancer-facts-and-figures/2025/2025-cancer-facts-and-figures-acs.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e8bfdfa3542806c6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTable 4. Incidence Rates for Selected Cancers by State, US, 2017-2021 ... Dist. of Columbia ... Rates are per 100,000, age adjusted to the 2000 US standard population using 19 age groups, and adjusted for delays in case reporting. aExcludes appendix.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e8bfdfa3542806c6\">>>", "siteName": "www.cancer.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9ac6dc4b53b89678\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCancer statistics, 2025 - PubMed\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9ac6dc4b53b89678\">>>", "url": "https://pubmed.