o see statistics for a specific state, go to the State Cancer Profiles. The statistics presented in these stat facts are based on the most recent data available, most of which can be found in SEER*Explorer. In some cases, different year spans may be used.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"45e1b5bbc48a4c10\">>>", "siteName": "seer.cancer.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3ecc31412211ea63\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nUnited States Cancer Statistics (USCS) | U.S. Cancer Statistics | CDC\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3ecc31412211ea63\">>>", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/united-states-cancer-statistics/index.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fa70395c85b89429\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nResearchers can analyze high-quality cancer incidence data on the United States population. May 29, 2025 · About U.S. Cancer Statistics · U.S. Cancer Statistics provide data on more than 39 million new cancer cases and deaths.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fa70395c85b89429\">>>", "published": "June 10, 2025", "siteName": "www.cdc.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6b03d8a1099be760\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCancer statistics, 2024 - PubMed\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6b03d8a1099be760\">>>", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38230766/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"11eb57d20ba83df7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIncidence rates increased during 2015-2019 by 0.6%-1% annually for <strong>breast, pancreas, and uterine corpus cancers</strong> and by 2%-3% annually for prostate, liver (female), kidney, and human papillomavirus-associated oral cancers and for melanoma.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"11eb57d20ba83df7\">>>", "siteName": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"13901efbdfbd0e0b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGlobal cancer data by country | World Cancer Research Fund\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"13901efbdfbd0e0b\">>>", "url": "https://www.wcrf.org/preventing-cancer/cancer-statistics/global-cancer-data-by-country/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"efea2b1914a563ff\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSo, for example, an ASR of 10 in a population of 100,000 = 10 cases of cancer, but an ASR of 1 in a population of 10 million = 100 cases. For each of the site-specific cancers we report, we have provided a table of the top 5 countries by ASR and then a table for yearly incidence (new cases).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"efea2b1914a563ff\">>>", "published": "July 28, 2025", "siteName": "www.wcrf.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"673f8cd9c922d8ae\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCancer Facts and Statistics | American Cancer Society\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"673f8cd9c922d8ae\">>>", "url": "https://www.cancer.org/research/cancer-facts-statistics.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1e78b47a2ac91442\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe American Cancer Society (ACS) projects the numbers of new cancer cases and deaths expected each year to estimate the contemporary cancer burden because cancer incidence and mortality data lag 2 to 4 years behind the current year. The regularly updated Facts &amp; Figures publications present the most current trends in cancer occurrence and survival, as well as information on symptoms, prevention, early detection, and treatment. ... ACS has published Cancer Facts &amp; Figures annually since 1951.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1e78b47a2ac91442\">>>", "siteName": "www.cancer.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775274800679}}
{"type": "message", "id": "9bf18494", "parentId": "1feae2c7", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T03:53:20.680Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_521e73872a434d7d963977af", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"lung cancer 5-year survival rate 2024 2025 statistics\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 937,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6a12fc999fd6b85a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLung Cancer Survival Rates | 5-Year Survival Rates for Lung Cancer | American Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6a12fc999fd6b85a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/lung-cancer/detection-diagnosis-staging/survival-rates.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a18110119a98b578\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFor example, if the 5-year relative survival rate for a specific stage of lung cancer is 60%, it means that people who have that cancer are, on average, <strong>about 60%</strong> as likely as people who don’t have that cancer to live for at least 5 years after being diagnosed.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a18110119a98b578\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e9fc3c550c51468\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLung and Bronchus Cancer — Cancer Stat Facts - SEER\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e9fc3c550c51468\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/lungb.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c37d8d708a3e8b51\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLung and bronchus cancer represents 11.1% of all new cancer cases in the U.S. ... In 2025, it is estimated that there will be 226,650 new cases of lung and bronchus cancer and an estimated <strong>124,730 people will die of this disease</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c37d8d708a3e8b51\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seer.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca0de33bc8fc2c34\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nPredicting Lung Cancer Survival to the Future: Population-Based Cancer Survival Modeling Study - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca0de33bc8fc2c34\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11179019/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"35d77d825b8d0595\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLung cancer remains the leading cause of cancer-related mortality globally, with late diagnoses often resulting in poor prognosis. In response, <strong>the Lung Ambition Alliance aims to double the 5-year survival rate by 2025</strong>. Using the Taiwan Cancer ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"35d77d825b8d0595\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"95fd15f62ee01981\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNew Report: Lung Cancer Survival Rate Improves, But Gaps in Biomarker Testing and Lack of Screening | American Lung Association\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"95fd15f62ee01981\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.lung.org/media/press-releases/state-of-lung-cancer-2024\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d160eab47d5f8505\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLung cancer is the leading cause of the cancer deaths in the U.S., but the American Lung Association’s 2024 “State of Lung Cancer” report reveals positive news. The lung cancer survival rate has <strong>improved 26% in the last five years</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d160eab47d5f8505\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.lung.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a9f320a231a625dc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nState of Lung Cancer | Key Findings | American Lung Association\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a9f320a231a625dc\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.lung.org/research/state-of-lung-cancer/key-findings\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fe66095d3a122f1c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe 2025 “State of the Air” ... ... The lung cancer survival rate increased 26% over the last five years nationally to <strong>29.7%</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fe66095d3a122f1c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 5, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.lung.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "lung cancer 5-year survival rate 2024 2025 statistics", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 937, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6a12fc999fd6b85a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLung Cancer Survival Rates | 5-Year Survival Rates for Lung Cancer | American Cancer Society\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6a12fc999fd6b85a\">>>", "url": "https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/lung-cancer/detection-diagnosis-staging/survival-rates.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a18110119a98b578\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFor example, if the 5-year relative survival rate for a specific stage of lung cancer is 60%, it means that people who have that cancer are, on average, <strong>about 60%</strong> as likely as people who don’t have that cancer to live for at least 5 years after being diagnosed.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a18110119a98b578\">>>", "siteName": "www.cancer.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8e9fc3c550c51468\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLung and Bronchus Cancer — Cancer Stat Facts - SEER\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8e9fc3c550c51468\">>>", "url": "https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/lungb.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c37d8d708a3e8b51\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLung and bronchus cancer represents 11.1% of all new cancer cases in the U.S. ... In 2025, it is estimated that there will be 226,650 new cases of lung and bronchus cancer and an estimated <strong>124,730 people will die of this disease</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c37d8d708a3e8b51\">>>", "siteName": "seer.cancer.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ca0de33bc8fc2c34\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nPredicting Lung Cancer Survival to the Future: Population-Based Cancer Survival Modeling Study - PMC\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ca0de33bc8fc2c34\">>>", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11179019/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"35d77d825b8d0595\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLung cancer remains the leading cause of cancer-related mortality globally, with late diagnoses often resulting in poor prognosis. In response, <strong>the Lung Ambition Alliance aims to double the 5-year survival rate by 2025</strong>. Using the Taiwan Cancer ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"35d77d825b8d0595\">>>", "siteName": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"95fd15f62ee01981\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNew Report: Lung Cancer Survival Rate Improves, But Gaps in Biomarker Testing and Lack of Screening | American Lung Association\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"95fd15f62ee01981\">>>", "url": "https://www.lung.org/media/press-releases/state-of-lung-cancer-2024", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d160eab47d5f8505\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLung cancer is the leading cause of the cancer deaths in the U.S., but the American Lung Association’s 2024 “State of Lung Cancer” report reveals positive news. The lung cancer survival rate has <strong>improved 26% in the last five years</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d160eab47d5f8505\">>>", "siteName": "www.lung.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a9f320a231a625dc\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nState of Lung Cancer | Key Findings | American Lung Association\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a9f320a231a625dc\">>>", "url": "https://www.lung.org/research/state-of-lung-cancer/key-findings", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fe66095d3a122f1c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe 2025 “State of the Air” ... ... The lung cancer survival rate increased 26% over the last five years nationally to <strong>29.7%</strong>....\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fe66095d3a122f1c\">>>", "published": "February 5, 2026", "siteName": "www.lung.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775274800679}}
{"type": "message", "id": "a25e79e9", "parentId": "9bf18494", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T03:53:20.682Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_f33401b04d9c46d5ac0556f3", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"liver cancer 5-year survival rate statistics 2024\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 936,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"769b531d10731204\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLiver Cancer Survival Rates | American Cancer Society | American Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"769b531d10731204\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/liver-cancer/detection-diagnosis-staging/survival-rates.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"829877f7be0e96b0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFor example, studies have shown ... people with early-stage liver cancers who have a liver transplant, the 5-year survival rate is in the range of <strong>60% to 70%</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"829877f7be0e96b0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"75bfa3a4f98a578f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer of the Liver and Intrahepatic Bile Duct - Cancer Stat Facts\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"75bfa3a4f98a578f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/livibd.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e84ce4f57659601c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe earlier liver and intrahepatic ... The 5-year relative survival for localized liver and intrahepatic bile duct cancer is <strong>37.6%</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e84ce4f57659601c\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seer.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9af7ca696e4a21e0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLiver Cancer Survival Rates | Roswell Park Comprehensive Cancer Center - Buffalo, NY\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9af7ca696e4a21e0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.roswellpark.org/cancer/liver/survival-rates\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ed67a22235a94c5b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDistant disease. Among patients with disease that has spread to distant body areas at the time of diagnosis, 5-year survival is <strong>3.5%</strong>. Learn more liver cancer survival statistics from the National Cancer Institute.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ed67a22235a94c5b\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.roswellpark.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"db40194387482d1f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLife expectancy of patients with hepatocellular carcinoma according to the upfront treatment: A nationwide analysis - ScienceDirect\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"db40194387482d1f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2211568423000025\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ac9554d03823fd57\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTumor ablation (n = 5306), open resection (n = 5171), and minimally-invasive resection (n = 1833) achieved 5-year survival rates of <strong>53.8% (95% CI: 52.3–55.4), 54.1% (95% CI: 52.6–55.6), and 66.2% (95% CI: 63.7–68.7),</strong> respectively, with ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ac9554d03823fd57\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 20, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.sciencedirect.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7a692bfd4bc6e129\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSurvival Rates » Hepatitis B Foundation\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7a692bfd4bc6e129\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.hepb.org/research-and-programs/liver/staging-of-liver-cancer/survival-rates/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ad73909a71111443\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe 5-year survival rate from liver cancer varies from about <strong>10% to 14%</strong>. This survival rate is low partly because many people with liver cancer also have cirrhosis, which itself is a serious liver disease.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ad73909a71111443\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.hepb.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "liver cancer 5-year survival rate statistics 2024", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 936, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"769b531d10731204\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLiver Cancer Survival Rates | American Cancer Society | American Cancer Society\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"769b531d10731204\">>>", "url": "https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/liver-cancer/detection-diagnosis-staging/survival-rates.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"829877f7be0e96b0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFor example, studies have shown ... people with early-stage liver cancers who have a liver transplant, the 5-year survival rate is in the range of <strong>60% to 70%</strong>....\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"829877f7be0e96b0\">>>", "siteName": "www.cancer.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"75bfa3a4f98a578f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCancer of the Liver and Intrahepatic Bile Duct - Cancer Stat Facts\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"75bfa3a4f98a578f\">>>", "url": "https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/livibd.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e84ce4f57659601c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\