</strong> [1]. In Canada, it is the seventh most common cancer in women, with 6600 new cases in 2024 [2]. Despite ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"aa603142a26c56ce\">>>", "published": "April 24, 2025", "siteName": "www.mdpi.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9c0527bfb5f3cd7e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAnnual Report to the Nation 2025: National Cancer Statistics\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9c0527bfb5f3cd7e\">>>", "url": "https://seer.cancer.gov/report_to_nation/stats.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7c6b9feaa309bc27\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe Annual Report to the Nation on the Status of Cancer published statistics on new cancer cases, deaths, and trends in the United States. The report includes long-term trends since 2001 and short-term trends with the most recent five years of data, which covers 2017 – 2021 for incidence and 2018 – 2022 for mortality.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7c6b9feaa309bc27\">>>", "siteName": "seer.cancer.gov"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775274813171}}
{"type": "message", "id": "dfccb641", "parentId": "9612174f", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T03:53:33.174Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_f9712831b5344874bf064c50", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"pediatric cancer leukemia annual cases US children\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 980,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b60969f401be8d3a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer Stat Facts: Childhood Leukemia (Ages 0–19) - SEER\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b60969f401be8d3a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/childleuk.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e0caaca4c51ad9b0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRates of new cases are also referred to as incidence rates. View Data Table ... Rate of New Cases and Deaths per 100,000: The rate of new cases of childhood leukemia was <strong>4.8 per 100,000 children per year</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e0caaca4c51ad9b0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seer.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"04a56d4ebd090b69\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nKey Statistics for Childhood Leukemia | American Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"04a56d4ebd090b69\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/leukemia-in-children/key-statistics.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"72c5b3092d40eeae\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>About 3 in 4 leukemias among children and teens are acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL).</strong> Most of the remaining cases are acute myeloid leukemia (AML).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTE